---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Fixture from "../components/Fixture.astro";
---
<Base title="The interface starts here" description="iVOLT is a hybrid CSS/HTML/JS frontend framework: semantic components, a finite utility set, design tokens and optional JavaScript. Alpha." sidebar={false}>
  <section class="docs-hero">
    <div>
      <span class="docs-alpha">v0.1 alpha</span>
      <h1>The interface starts here.</h1>
      <p class="iv-u-text-lg iv-u-text-muted">Semantic components as the fast path, a finite set of utilities for composition, tokens as the visual contract and optional JavaScript for behaviour. No runtime dependencies. Works from a plain <code>&lt;link&gt;</code>, WordPress, Astro or any bundler.</p>
      <div class="iv-cluster">
        <a class="iv-button iv-button--primary iv-button--lg" href="/getting-started">Get started</a>
        <a class="iv-button iv-button--secondary iv-button--lg" href="/components/button">Components</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Fixture name="dialog/basic" title="Live: dialog with a form" />
  </section>

  <section class="docs-prose">
    <h2>Quick start (local files, no build)</h2>
    <p>The package is not published yet. Build it from the repository, copy <code>dist/</code> next to your page and link two files. The plain HTML starter in <code>examples/plain-html</code> is exactly this.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;html class="iv-root" data-iv-theme="system"&gt;
  &lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="ivolt/css/ivolt.min.css"&gt;
  &lt;script type="module" src="ivolt/js/auto.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
    <p><code>auto.js</code> is the only entry that initialises components on load. Import <code>index.js</code> instead when you want to call <code>init()</code> yourself.</p>

    <h2>Components in v0.1</h2>
    <p>Seven content families that need no JavaScript and six interactive ones that enhance real HTML. Each page has a live preview, the copyable HTML, options, events, keyboard behaviour and the no-JS fallback.</p>
    <nav class="docs-components" aria-label="Components">
      {["button", "card", "form", "badge", "alert", "table", "breadcrumb", "pagination", "progress", "skeleton", "disclosure", "tabs", "dialog", "drawer", "dropdown", "toast"].map((c) => <a href={`/components/${c}`}>{c[0].toUpperCase() + c.slice(1)}</a>)}
    </nav>

    <h2>Foundations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/foundations/tokens-and-themes">Tokens and themes</a>: every visual decision as a <code>--iv-*</code> custom property, light/dark/system scopes without JavaScript.</li>
      <li><a href="/foundations/layout">Layout and utilities</a>: container, stack, cluster, grid and a finite, generated utility matrix.</li>
      <li><a href="/foundations/typography">Typography</a>, <a href="/foundations/accessibility">accessibility</a> and <a href="/foundations/coexistence">coexisting with existing CSS</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Recipes</h2>
    <p>Three complete pages built only with the package: a <a href="/examples/landing/index.html">business landing</a>, an <a href="/examples/catalog/index.html">editorial catalogue</a> with working filters, and a <a href="/examples/admin/index.html">static admin panel</a>. <a href="/examples">Open or download them</a>, or try the <a href="/playground">playground</a> to generate snippets.</p>

    <h2>Distribution</h2>
    <p>Layered and flat CSS, one CSS file per component, ES modules with real <code>exports</code>, an IIFE with a single <code>IVOLT</code> global, type declarations and the token JSON. Sizes are measured per artifact and published with their method in the repository.</p>

    <h2>Themes</h2>
    <p>Set <code>data-iv-theme</code> to <code>light</code>, <code>dark</code> or <code>system</code> on any element. Explicit choices win over the system preference, scopes nest, and nothing requires JavaScript or storage.</p>
    <Fixture name="theme/nested" title="Nested theme scopes" />

    <h2>Status and honesty</h2>
    <p>Alpha: APIs may change before 0.1.0. Sizes, browser support and accessibility results are only published with their method, version and commit. There are no benchmarks against other frameworks.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
